{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546843-things-you-like-from-other-game-systems","id":1546843,"title":"Things you like from other game systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-10T10:22:44-08:00","id":1546843,"title":"Things you like from other game systems","content":"While we all love (and hate) the Storyteller System, there are countless other game frameworks around, with their perks. Have you ever taken something from them and used it at your table? Or at least wanted to do it but without any success? Not simply an home rule (&quot;at my table we add health levels with high stamina&quot;): a deliberate act of inspiration from another framework.<br /> <br /> Like, for example, the flashback mechanic from Blades in the Dark. Or a particular magic system. Or fight order system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T15:54:21-08:00","id":1546851,"title":"","content":"I use a lot of stuff from GURPS. In particular, I use Gurps Thaumatology to custom tailor the Spheres to my liking, to the point that my games no longer have 9 Spheres, and not even there's a fixed amount. Each one of my magic groups has their very own unique system of Spheres, with their own variable numbers. My Dreamspeakers for example only recognize 3 &quot;Spheres&quot; (they actually call them &quot;Realms&quot;), which are Body, Spirit and Mind. The Technocrats have 7 Spheres and many many other variations.<br /> <br /> I also use it for creating &quot;Sub-Spheres&quot;. For instance, &quot;Plant Magic&quot; or &quot;Pyrocinesis&quot;. Thus, Mages on my table can become specialists in plant magic instead of having to learn everything about life, or being a &quot;Fire Wizard&quot; exclusively instead of dealing with everything of Forces. That goes way, way deep, for instance allowing Empaths (Mages that deal with emotions), Telepaths, Seers, &quot;Ice Mages&quot;, &quot;Thunder Mages&quot;, &quot;Metamorphs&quot;, Necromancers and many many other variations, allowing Mages to get a lot more bang for a much stricter area","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}